 highest on the page, and OPEN is next at 61.5. OPEN, QNT, BROS and BLDR are bouncing inside longer declines. OPEN is -9.9% over one month and -48.0% over three months, but it rose 16.0% on the day. QNT is -32.7% and -36.0%, with an 11.0% up day. BROS is +2.4% over one month but -37.9% over three months; BLDR is -6.9% and -26.1%. One strong day is not a turn while the month stays lower. Two names need a different reading. CTVA's -84.2% 1-month and -85.2% 3-month returns are a mechanical price adjustment, not a collapse: Corteva moved its seed and genetics business into Vylor Inc. on 1 October 2026, so the quoted price fell about 84% and its RoC of +12.09 is not comparable with its own history unless the base is restated ([Corteva/Vylor spin-off and the October 2026 price adjustment](https://tickeron.com/blogs/corteva-ctva-drops-86-in-30-days-following-vylor-spinoff-17581/), [Corteva spin-off and court challenge](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2128626/000119312526419727/d170287d8k.htm)). A court challenge briefly blocked dividends and buybacks before a stay. QNT is Quantinuum, which priced an upsized IPO on 3 June 2026, began trading on Nasdaq on 4 June 2026 and raised $1.68 billion at an implied valuation near $15.7 billion ([Quantinuum IPO — June 4, 2026](https://www.quantinuum.com/press-releases/quantinuum-announces-pricing-of-upsized-initial-public-offering)). Its -32.7% one-month move is a fade from a short listing history, not a long downtrend. RXO has the fastest RoC on the page (+185.6) and +44.2% over one month, but only +0.6% over three months and the widest trend-fit gap (0.99): a spike, not an established trend. The other scores cluster between 47.9 and 53.0, too narrow for the order inside that band to carry meaning."}},"research_scope":{"business_focus":"","forecast_windows":[{"end_utc":"2026-10-23T07:16:04.413225+00:00","horizon":"1 Week","start_utc":"2026-10-16T07:16:04.413225+00:00"},{"end_utc":"2026-11-15T07:16:04.413225+00:00","horizon":"1